Because there are **two different “statuses”** in the docs system:

1) **Doc lifecycle status** = `frontmatter.facets.status`  
- `/docs` **Status dropdown** filters on *this* value:

```237:240:/home/broz/code/rockcap/src/app/docs/page.tsx
  const filteredDocs = manifest.docs
    .filter((doc) => {
      if (selectedType !== "all" && doc.facets.type !== selectedType) return false;
      if (selectedStatus !== "all" && doc.facets.status !== selectedStatus) return false;
```

…and `/docs` defaults that dropdown to **active**:

```75:80:/home/broz/code/rockcap/src/app/docs/page.tsx
  // Default to "active" status when arriving from docs route (no status param)
  const status = searchParams.get("status") || "active";
```

So for a bug ticket to show up under the default Status filter, its **frontmatter** must be `facets.status: active`.

2) **Ticket workflow status badge** = the **`Status:` line in the markdown body**  
The manifest extracts that separately as `ticketStatus`:

```70:80:/home/broz/code/rockcap/src/app/api/docs/manifest/route.ts
function extractTicketStatus(body: string): string | undefined {
  const match = body.match(/^Status:\s*([^\n<]+)\s*(?:<|$)/im);
  // ...
  return raw.replace(/\s+/g, " ");
}
```

…and includes it on the doc metadata:

```140:160:/home/broz/code/rockcap/src/app/api/docs/manifest/route.ts
const isTicket = Array.isArray(frontmatter?.tags) && frontmatter.tags.includes("plan/ticket");
const ticketStatus = isTicket ? extractTicketStatus(body) : undefined;

const doc: DocMetadata = {
  // ...
  ...(ticketStatus ? { ticketStatus } : {}),
  facets: { status: frontmatter?.facets?.status || "active", /* ... */ },
};
```

**So you can have:** `facets.status: active` (so it passes the Status dropdown filter) **while still showing a “Done” badge** because the body contains `Status: Done`.
